From 54dcca43912135f5b2e98f014f233a00a0a31558 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 07:44:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [sensorfwd] Preload sensors listed in "preload_sensors"
 config key

When a Qt6 client opens a sensor through the libqtsensors_sensorfw
plugin (e.g. QAmbientLightSensor through luna-sysmgr), the plugin calls
requestSensor() directly on /SensorManager over D-Bus. On a build that
ships neither contextprovider-1.0 (the only path that preloads
ContextSensor + ALSSensor in main.cpp today) nor a Halium hwconfig
asserting Feature_* defaults, no sensor plugin is auto-loaded and the
first requestSensor() fails with:

    SensorManagerError: "requested sensor id 'alssensor' not registered"

The client never recovers because the failure looks like a permanent
unsupported-sensor error rather than a "not loaded yet" condition.

Add a small comma-separated "preload_sensors" config key that an
integrator can drop into a device's sensord conf, and call
SensorManager::loadPlugin() for each name right after the manager comes
up. The list is read through the existing SensorFrameworkConfig so it
inherits the regular sensord.conf.d merging order; unknown names just
log a "-> failed" line and otherwise stay out of the way.

Suggested device conf:

    preload_sensors=alssensor,accelerometersensor,gyroscopesensor,\
                    magnetometersensor,orientationsensor

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 sensord/main.cpp | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sensord/main.cpp b/sensord/main.cpp
index e43ecd1..22b32b7 100644
--- a/sensord/main.cpp
+++ b/sensord/main.cpp
@@ -281,6 +281,44 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
     }
 #endif
 
+    /*
+     * Preload sensors named in the "preload_sensors" config key. This is
+     * a comma-separated list of sensor plugin names; each is loaded right
+     * after SensorManager comes up so that requestSensor() over D-Bus can
+     * succeed immediately on first call, without the client having to
+     * fall back to loadPlugin() explicitly.
+     *
+     * Without this, sensors whose Q[Type]Sensor Qt6 backend goes straight
+     * to requestSensor() (e.g. QAmbientLightSensor through
+     * libqtsensors_sensorfw.so) report "requested sensor id '<name>' not
+     * registered" on the first call, because lazy plugin loading in
+     * sensorfwd currently only fires for the magnetometer (via the
+     * --magnetometer-bg-calibration path) and for the ContextSensor
+     * path (only compiled when PROVIDE_CONTEXT_INFO is set, which in
+     * turn requires the legacy contextprovider-1.0 package).
+     *
+     * Builds that ship neither contextprovider nor the Halium-style
+     * hwconfig defaults end up with no auto-loaded sensors at all, so
+     * the on-demand request path is the only one available -- and on
+     * the current sensorfw it does not register the plugin.
+     *
+     * Example device conf:
+     *   preload_sensors=alssensor,accelerometersensor,gyroscopesensor
+     */
+    {
+        const QString preload =
+            SensorFrameworkConfig::configuration()->value<QString>("preload_sensors");
+        const QStringList names = preload.split(QLatin1Char(','));
+        for (const QString &item : names) {
+            const QString name = item.trimmed();
+            if (name.isEmpty())
+                continue;
+            const bool ok = sm.loadPlugin(name);
+            qCInfo(lcSensorFw) << "Preloading sensor" << name
+                               << (ok ? "-> ok" : "-> failed");
+        }
+    }
+
     if (parser.magnetometerCalibration()) {
         CalibrationHandler* calibrationHandler_ = new CalibrationHandler(nullptr);
         calibrationHandler_->initiateSession();
-- 
